From 9d5195a55ae0ab53f6bee7688d3fe8fe3f00a237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Dahunsi <dahunsisamuel1st@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:58:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Org map: add privacy-lab (private research workspace)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New repo for the privacy track's feasibility work, per the privacy strategy
§12: experiments stay outside the consensus-critical chain path so research
code cannot quietly become production architecture.

Private, and bound by Appendix A's guardrails — no x/privacy, no consensus or
ante-handler changes, no forks of the four upstream repos, nothing vendored.
konstellation remains the only repo that produces a binary.

- ENGINEERING.md §5: row in the org map
- CLAUDE.md: row in the repo table

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CLAUDE.md      | 1 +
 ENGINEERING.md | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md
index 3f7e4ea..3e7fe61 100644
--- a/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/CLAUDE.md
@@ -51,4 +51,5 @@ find something the next agent must know. Convert relative dates to absolute.
 | `whitepaper` | versioned PDF releases |
 | `chain-config` | npm package for dapp developers |
 | `faucet` | testnet token faucet |
+| `privacy-lab` | privacy research — private; never consensus code, nothing ships |
 | `.github` | org-wide CODEOWNERS and shared workflows |
diff --git a/ENGINEERING.md b/ENGINEERING.md
index 21fbd1b..b5c63b8 100644
--- a/ENGINEERING.md
+++ b/ENGINEERING.md
@@ -273,6 +273,7 @@ konstellation-network/
 │
 ├── chain-config           ← npm package for dapp devs. Public. (pre-mainnet)
 ├── faucet                 ← testnet token faucet. Public. (pre-mainnet)
+├── privacy-lab            ← privacy research. PRIVATE. Never consensus code, never ships.
 └── .github                ← shared workflows, CODEOWNERS template. (pre-mainnet)
                              (CODEOWNERS itself is per-repo — GitHub has no
                              org-wide default for it; see §17.)
